WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
答案摆在眼前，很容易觉得自己已经会了。
With the answer in sight, it is easy to feel that you know it.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.000
现在合上纸页，试着自己说出来。
Now fold the page shut and try to recall it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.700
先找答案，再打开核对。这就是一次提取练习。
Retrieve the answer before reopening the page to check it.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.000
忘了的地方圈出来，下一次只多练这个缺口。
Mark the missing piece and practice it again.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.700
一项实验比较了重读和回忆练习。
An experiment compared rereading and retrieval practice.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:28.100
五分钟后，重读过的文章记得更多。
After five minutes, reread passages were remembered better.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:34.000
两天或一周后，练过回忆的文章保留更多。
After two days or one week, recall-practiced passages were retained better.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
把两道回忆题接在每天收书包这个固定动作后面。
Attach two recall questions to a regular action like packing your bag.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.000
稳定情境里的反复行动，有助于形成习惯。
Repetition in a stable context helps build a habit.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.600
睡眠也参与学习后的记忆巩固。
Sleep also participates in memory consolidation after learning.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:55.000
给学习留下一段正常的睡眠时间，第二天再检索一次。
Leave time for normal sleep, then retrieve again the next day.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.800
今天先回忆并核对，明天不看答案再试一次。
Recall and check today. Try again tomorrow without the answer.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.000
几天后能自己想起，比刚看过时的熟悉感更有用。
Being able to recall it days later is more informative than immediate familiarity.
